<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3325" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ărăcynthus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀράκυνθος</span>.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A mountain in Ætolia</i> (acc. to some,
			in Acarnania), now <i>Zygos</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 2, 3,
				§ 6</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A mountain between Bœotia and Attica</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Prop. 4, 14, 42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 2,
				239</span></i>; with the epithet Actaeus (<i>Attic</i>), <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 2, 24</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
